s":30},"commit_author":{"id":218610,"login":"trask"},"deadline":1791442930,"findings":[{"body":"<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\n\n### \ud83d\udd35 Needs a closer look\n\nThe README and changelog overstate the coroutine behavior by including default-enabled Flow-returning `@WithSpan` methods.\n\n**0 open findings**\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>1 resolved since last review</strong></summary>\n\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Low severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Clarify selector scope versus Flow support in module metadata](#discussion_r4214348398)\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Previously missed (2)</strong></summary>\n\nIn code that hasn't changed since last review\n\n<details>\n<summary><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Low severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> Narrow migration note to suspend-function instrumentation</summary>\n\n`CHANGELOG.md:10`\n\n[General] The migration note currently implies that all Kotlin coroutine `@WithSpan` behavior becomes default-off. Only suspend-function instrumentation changes default; Flow-returning methods remain covered by the default-enabled generic annotation instrumentation. Name the narrower behavior here so the breaking-change guidance is accurate.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Low severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> Clarify default-off scope for Kotlin suspend instrumentation</summary>\n\n`instrumentation/\u200bkotlinx-coroutines/\u200bREADME.md:8`\n\n[General] This wording is broader than the behavior being changed. The default-off module instruments only Kotlin suspend functions; `@WithSpan` methods returning `Flow` are still instrumented by the generic annotation module by default (the Flow module only supplies asynchronous completion). Qualify both statements so users do not expect all coroutine-related `@WithSpan` spans to disappear.\n</details>\n</details>\n\n\ud83e\udde0 **Review effort:** Balanced\n\n---\n\nGive feedback about Copilot approvals in [this survey](https://survey.alchemer.com/s3/9011660/CCR-Public-Preview-Autoapprove-feedback-survey) to enter a drawing for a $150 gift card.","comment_id":null,"key":"review:5451334406","kind":"body","line":null,"path":null,"review_id":5451334406},{"body":"<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\n\n### \ud83d\udfe2 Approval recommended\n\nThe default changes, selector isolation, tests, and migration documentation are consistent and complete.\n\n**0 open findings**\n\n\ud83e\udde0 **Review effort:** Balanced\n\n---\n\nGive feedback about Copilot approvals in [this survey](https://survey.alchemer.com/s3/9011660/CCR-Public-Preview-Autoapprove-feedback-survey) to enter a drawing for a $150 gift card.","comment_id":null,"key":"review:5451390943","kind":"body","line":null,"path":null,"review_id":54513